  "settingsDiagnosticsTitle": "Diagnostic",
  "@settingsDiagnosticsTitle": {
    "description": "Title of the Diagnostics screen and of its tile on the Settings screen. Holds the switch for sharing failures with the developers, and below it the log of errors and warnings this device recorded. Was called \"Log\" before the switch was added."
  },
  "settingsDiagnosticsSubtitle": "Partager les échecs et lire le journal",
  "@settingsDiagnosticsSubtitle": {
    "description": "Subtitle under the Diagnostics tile on the Settings screen. Names both halves of the screen: the sharing switch and the recorded log."
  },
  "diagnosticsShareTitle": "Partager les journaux avec les développeurs",
  "@diagnosticsShareTitle": {
    "description": "Label of the switch that decides whether errors and crashes are sent to the developers. On by default. Phrased as what the user gets rather than as the name of a service, because the service is an implementation detail that may change."
  },
  "diagnosticsShareSubtitle": "Les erreurs et les plantages sont envoyés automatiquement afin de pouvoir être corrigés. Aucune donnée de carte, clé ou capture n’est jamais envoyée.",
  "@diagnosticsShareSubtitle": {
    "description": "Explains the switch above it. Two facts, in the order a user asks them: that sending needs no action from them, and what is never included. The second half matters because this app handles card dumps, keys and radio captures, and the user has no way to verify the claim themselves."
  },
  "diagnosticsReplayTitle": "Inclure un enregistrement de l’écran",
  "@diagnosticsReplayTitle": {
    "description": "Label of the second switch on the Diagnostics screen, below the sharing switch and shown only while sharing is on. Decides whether a recording of the screen is kept and sent when something fails. On by default, and only ever active on Android and iOS. \"Replay\" is what the service calls it; the label says what it is instead, because the user has no reason to know the term."
  },
  "diagnosticsReplaySubtitle": "L’enregistrement tourne tant que l’application est ouverte et ne quitte votre appareil que lorsque quelque chose échoue. Les octets des cartes, les tracés de signaux et l’écran du Flipper y sont masqués.",
  "@diagnosticsReplaySubtitle": {
    "description": "Explains the switch above it. Three facts in the order a user asks them: that recording is continuous, that the recording only leaves the device on a failure, and what stays hidden even then. The first is deliberate and must survive translation - the sample rate gates the upload, not the capture, so a user reading only the switch label would think nothing is recorded until something breaks. The third is a promise three masking rules keep rather than a reassurance. Renders at up to six lines and ellipsises after that, so if the translation runs long, keep the first and third facts ahead of the second. \"Hidden\" rather than \"blacked out\": the mask is painted in the theme's primary colour, not black."
  },
  "diagnosticsNoticeTitle": "Les échecs sont partagés avec les développeurs",
  "@diagnosticsNoticeTitle": {
    "description": "Heading of the one-time notice shown on the first launch, and once more for people already using the app when sharing was added. States the fact rather than asking a question, because reporting is already on while the notice is on screen - it is a notice, not a consent prompt."
  },
  "diagnosticsNoticeBody": "Lorsque quelque chose échoue, l’erreur et le plantage sont envoyés seuls, avec la version de l’application et la build dont elle provient. Sur Android et iOS, un enregistrement de l’écran les accompagne. Les données de cartes, les clés, les captures et votre position y sont masquées et ne sont jamais envoyées. Vous pouvez désactiver cela maintenant ou à tout moment dans Paramètres → Diagnostic.",
  "@diagnosticsNoticeBody": {
    "description": "Body of the one-time notice. Four things in the order a user asks them: what is sent, that a screen recording is part of it, what never is, and how to stop it. The recording sentence names the two platforms because replay is native-backed and does nothing on desktop, so saying it unconditionally would be false for most desktop users. \"Hidden from that recording\" is a claim five masking rules keep, not a reassurance - keep it attached to the recording sentence in translation, because apart they read as two unrelated promises. No link to a privacy policy, because the project has none yet; the text carries the substance instead."
  },
  "diagnosticsNoticeTurnOff": "Désactiver",
  "@diagnosticsNoticeTurnOff": {
    "description": "The dismissing action on the one-time notice that also turns sharing off. Present so that opting out costs one tap at the moment the user is being told, rather than a hunt through Settings afterwards."
  },
